# Cursor team (City Day)

Shared product rules, flow, and claiming live in `CLAUDE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and `docs/SDLC.md`. Do not restate them here. The charter is [docs/reviews/2026-10-direction.md](../../docs/reviews/2026-10-direction.md) in this repo. Do not open any other repo.

## Cursor-only

- At session start, generate a team ID: `cursor-<4 hex chars>` (e.g. `echo cursor-$(openssl rand -hex 2)`). Put it in the Team log, every summary, `Question for PM:`, and the PR body.
- Roles live in `.cursor/agents/` (same names as `.claude/agents/`; Cursor prefers `.cursor/`).
- Only the Engineering Manager writes to GitHub (PR open/edit, and the one Team log comment). Other roles return results to the EM. The token cannot comment on issues or change labels. Do not try.
- Leave `.claude/` and `CLAUDE.md` alone unless a ticket says otherwise.
- Claim by opening a draft PR with `Closes #N` and one Team log comment, edited in place. The PM posts the proxy claim on the issue. Jake play-tests and merges. See [docs/SDLC.md#claiming-a-ticket](docs/SDLC.md#claiming-a-ticket).

## Model routing and fallback (spend policy)

- On-demand usage is OFF. Never pick a model that would need it.
- At session start the EM checks the usage dashboard and sets the mode:
  A = Other Models budget left; B = Other Models exhausted; C = Cursor Models >90% used.
- Every role runs on its committed pin in every mode: developer on
  grok-4.7[reasoning_effort=high,fast=false], tech-lead on grok-4.7 xhigh, the rest on
  Composer 2.5. Premium (Claude/GPT) is spent on quality gates and escalations, and
  only in mode A.
- The EM may not override a pin at launch except for an escalation trigger below.
  Log every override in the Team log as `override: pinned X -> Y, reason`.
- Fallback: Claude -> GPT -> grok-4.7[reasoning_effort=high,fast=false]
  -> cursor-grok-4.6-high -> composer-2.5[fast=false] -> stop and ask PM.
  Claude and GPT share one pool, so once it is empty go straight to Grok.
- Never use Auto to save money (it can route to third-party models). Always fast=false.
- Keep Grok 4.7 context under 256k.

## Quality gates

- Plan gate: before any implementation, a premium model approves the plan:
  claude-sonnet-5-5 in mode A, otherwise grok-4.7[reasoning_effort=xhigh,fast=false].
- Merge gate: before the PR is marked ready, a premium model reviews the full diff
  against the acceptance criteria. It must be a different model family from the developer.
- Escalation triggers: any failed test, a diff over ~300 lines, or a change touching
  auth, data, or payments goes to the premium gate reviewer early.
- Gates stay short and cheap: input is only the diff + acceptance criteria; output is
  only a verdict (pass, or fail with reasons). The EM logs the verdict and the model
  that actually ran on the Team log line.
- If the developer ran on Claude, the gate reviewer is gpt-5.6-terra or grok-4.7 xhigh,
  never Claude.
- Full policy: `docs/model-routing.md`.
